< **A design point found while specifying them.** Every number is at risk in every draw, so all numbers share the same number of draws. A score that depends only on a number's own count over the same draws is therefore a monotone function of that count, and gives exactly the ranking of counting over those draws. The plain textbook versions of E_7 and E_8 would rank exactly like E_1. A plain E_9 at E_6's forgetting rates would rank exactly like E_6's decay variants.
